			"customizationId": "spearm",
			"height": 188,
			"weight": 170,
			"backgroundStory": "Gu Yuanyue entered the sect at an age when most promising disciples had already begun making names for themselves. There was nothing remarkable about him. He had no rare constitution, no startling breakthrough, no master willing to declare that he was destined for greatness. He simply had enough talent to be accepted, and enough patience to remain. While the others were pulled aside for extra instruction and praised in front of the hall, he practiced the same forms until his hands stopped making mistakes, took whatever duties were given to him, and slowly became dependable in the quiet way that few people bother to praise.\r\n\r\nWhen the sect was destroyed, there was no heroic last stand or miraculous escape; he happened to be far enough from the worst of it, and knew when to leave. Years of being overlooked had made him accustomed to carrying on without anyone watching. At twenty-five, he still trains the way he always has: steadily, without expecting recognition. The sect is gone now, but every ordinary lesson it gave an ordinary disciple is still there in the way he moves.",
			"refuseText": "We have enough hands for now...",
			"acceptText": "We need someone reliable!",
